{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"level"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<level>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/level","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric"]]},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"level"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"level","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV5levelAA8MXLLevelVSgvp"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/level"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/level":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/level","title":"level","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/level","abstract":[{"text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lyric type represents text underlays for lyrics. Two text elements that are not separated by an elision"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and chorus."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"title":"MXLLyric"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLevel":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLLevel","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllevel","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The level type is used to specify editorial information for different MusicXML elements. The content contains"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifying and\/or descriptive text about the editorial status of the parent element."}]}}}